## Context

Three registers under `data/jetp/migration/` were left by the migration
train with rows that had no owner: `0876-pending.csv` (91 rows: 83
event-timing dispositions and 8 implementation events), the 5 pending rows of
`1160-citation-decisions.csv` (the same five events) and the 54 `no_referent`
rows of `0884-coverage-dispositions.csv` (37 authorities with no matching
party name, 17 project identifiers 0875 left unresolved). 145 distinct rows.

Homes approved by the author on 2026-09-29: unknown Senegal date roles are
resolved from the cited pages where the page supports a role, else left
pending with the reason refined; page-observation dates are terminal (author
decision 2026-09-24); the four unsupported physical claims of 1160 are
rejected; the Cirebon snapshot goes to [[0920]]; the 17 unresolved project
identifiers go to [[0833]] (M1b); an authority is covered by a party only where a
line justifies the party. Judgment rows (three 0970 holds, the AfDB approval
day, the MAF milestone, the Saloum tender deadline) are decided by the Fable
tier with a confidence; anything below the configured threshold goes to
`data/jetp/decisions.md` for the author (storage contract § 4).

## Method

- Every cited page was read from the pinned snapshot (pdftotext, HTML to
  text); no live source was fetched. Positive controls: the same reading
  found the ISLE-1 CAD 64.3 million row (Table 4.3-2), the Singkarak
  "temporarily halted" row (Table 4.3-3), the briquetting Projet #2 at
  EUR 0.3 million (plan p. 42) and the QW2 total EUR 215.9 million (p. 53).
- The record of every decision is `data/jetp/migration/1620-register-dispositions.csv`
  (one row per register row, 145 distinct keys, `decided_by`, confidence,
  page evidence). `0876-pending.csv` gains `disposition` and `owner`; resolved
  and rejected rows leave it and are accounted for in
  `0876-timing-reconciliation.csv` and `1160-citation-decisions.csv`.
- Party rule for the 37 authorities: R1 a party in force that publishes one of
  the row's own sources; R2 a party a register line names for the same
  organisation; R3 a composite row ("France and AFD") goes to the agency when
  R1 holds for it, else to the country; R4 a party is minted only from a line
  in force that prints its name, with the authority category of the legacy
  row and no external identifier (none is held in a snapshot line); R5
  otherwise left uncovered, naming the lines that would justify it.
- Threshold for tier decisions: `config/jetp_tracking.yaml`
  `matching.llm_adjudication.accept_threshold` (0.8).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Every row of the three registers has an owner or a recorded disposition in `1620-register-dispositions.csv` (145 distinct keys)
- [ ] The judgment rows carry decision, page evidence and confidence; those below the threshold are items in `data/jetp/decisions.md`
- [ ] Log notes and exit-criterion lines on [[0920]], [[0833]] and the M2 child that owns the unextracted Senelec notice index ([[1502]])
- [ ] `tests/test_jetp_register_dispositions.py` red before the data change, green after
- [ ] `make jetp-ledger-check`, `make check-fast`, `make lint` green; `make check-jetp` green on padme
- [ ] Served-view byte changes listed in the PR with a diff summary of the four country JSONs and the parties/names views
